# =============================================================================
# Python artifacts
# Byte-compiled caches, linter caches, packaging metadata, virtualenvs.
# pyproject.toml at the root is real config and stays tracked - it is not
# matched by any pattern below.
# =============================================================================
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# =============================================================================
# Codegraph index
# Per-machine code knowledge graph built by the codegraph CLI.
# =============================================================================
.codegraph/

# =============================================================================
# Pipeline runtime state
# SQLite run state and other per-machine pipeline artifacts.
# =============================================================================
.claude/state/

# =============================================================================
# Per-machine local settings
# May hold personal tokens or paths; never shared across machines.
# =============================================================================
.claude/settings.local.json

# =============================================================================
# Project work product (plans, specs, tasks, memory)
# These are generated while running a project through the pipeline and do not
# belong in the published template. Only the scaffolding a fresh clone needs
# (templates, contract docs, and the directory skeleton) is kept - see the
# negations below. Contents are excluded rather than the directory itself, so
# the negations can re-include specific files inside.
# =============================================================================
.claude/plans/
.claude/specs/*
.claude/memory/*
.claude/agent-memory/
.claude/project/*

# Memory layer contract survives for a fresh clone.
!.claude/memory/README.md

# Spec template survives for a fresh clone, same scaffolding role as
# .claude/tasks/templates/.
!.claude/specs/_template.md

# Project overlay contract, and every overlay document, survive for a fresh
# clone: rules/self-learning.md sends agents here to record project quirks, so a
# newly created .claude/project/quirks.md must be tracked, not silently dropped.
# Markdown only - anything else under the overlay stays excluded.
!.claude/project/*.md

# Task work product is excluded per-folder (not via .claude/tasks/) so the
# templates/ folder and the pipeline's directory skeleton stay tracked.
.claude/tasks/backlog/*
.claude/tasks/active/*
.claude/tasks/done/*
.claude/tasks/epics/*
.claude/tasks/handoffs/*

# Keep the empty-directory placeholders so git tracks the skeleton itself.
!.claude/tasks/backlog/.gitkeep
!.claude/tasks/active/.gitkeep
!.claude/tasks/done/.gitkeep
!.claude/tasks/epics/.gitkeep
!.claude/tasks/handoffs/.gitkeep
